 approve PKT-0069. The investigation answers the packet's question with measurements, and both problems from the last rejection are fixed.\n\n- **Goal:** the cache keyed by font, size, style, PPI and text was measured on a patched copy of sdkjs.\n  - **Measured:** x2t CPU dropped by 16–26% across three large sheets. All 521 pages of the 25k-row PDF came out pixel-identical. Memory use went up by 50–90 MB.\n  - **Verdict:** the diagnosis doc says the cache is worth carrying as a small patch or upstream PR, not a fork.\n  - **Not prototyped:** skipping measurement for numbers that fit. The log explains why: it changes the overflow and `###` logic.\n- **Contract:** the installed documentserver files were not touched; all work ran on a copy. The pixel comparison supports \"output stays visually identical\", at least for the 25k-row sample.\n- **Budget:** 5 files and 151 lines changed, within the limits of 6 files and 800 lines.\n- **TEP-0004 checks:** the Executor log is filled in. The follow-up request in `.theseus/spawn/` has no template placeholders left, and its acceptance commands can actually run.\n- **Surprises:** two are recorded in the log and the Lessons section: x2t loads `sdk-all.js`, not `sdk-all-min.js`, and the snapshot files make no speed difference. There's nothing that needs a test, since this is an investigation packet with no code target.\n\nWeaknesses that don't block approval:\n\n- **Few runs:** the numbers come from only 1–2 runs each on a shared VM. The doc says so and gives a range.\n- **Hit rate:** the patch counts cache hits and misses, but nobody read the counts, because x2t gives no way to print from inside the patch.\n- **Patch script comment:** the \"Stats:\" line in `sdkjs-shape-cache.py` is garbled.\n- **Follow-up's acceptance checks are weak:** they only check that files exist and the service answers. The real check (rebuild, measure, compare pages) lives only in the follow-up's goal text. Whoever reviews that packet will need to check 